<title>UK: UK card spending up yr/yr 27.3 pct in Aug - CCRG.</title>
<headline>UK card spending up yr/yr 27.3 pct in Aug - CCRG.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Credit Card Research Group, representing major UK credit and debit card issuers, released the following consumer spending figures for August 1996 -</p>
<p> CARD EXPENDITURE (in million stg) * Aug 96    Aug 95   % change</p>
<p> All sectors - total		     7,134     5,602    27.3</p>
<p> Food and drink			    1,836     1,405    30.7</p>
<p> Mixed business				539	 383    40.8</p>
<p> Clothing					435	 328    32.5</p>
<p> Household				     578	 437    32.2</p>
<p> Motoring					895	 823     8.8</p>
<p> Entertainment				 426	 319    33.6</p>
<p> Hotels					  298	 239    24.9</p>
<p> Travel					  815	 656    24.3</p>
<p> Services					540	 410    31.9</p>
<p>Credit Card Research Group director Elizabeth Philips said, &quot;These figures are extremely encouraging. Card spending is growing at a much faster rate than retail sales which shows that the consumer is choosing to pay by plastic more frequently, especially in the high street.&quot; NOTE * figures adjusted for variations in the number of processing days between months. -- London Newsroom +44 171 324 7715</p>
</text>
